 34S     33S(D,P)                      1972CR08,1971VA21,1963BR05ENSDF    202609
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  J|p=3/2+ for {+33}S ground state (2025Ch07).                           
 34S  c  1972Cr08: {+33}S(d,p) with a 12-MeV deuteron beam from the Argonne FN  
 34S 2c  tandem Van de Graaff accelerator. The target was 83%-enriched {+33}S   
 34S 3c  evaporated onto a 30-|mg/cm{+2} C foil and sandwiched beneath a second 
 34S 4c  C foil. Reaction protons were analyzed by an Enge split-pole magnetic  
 34S 5c  spectrograph and detected using nuclear track emulsions placed in the  
 34S 6c  focal plane. Measured |s(E{-p},|q) from 9|' to 59|' with FWHM=16 keV.  
 34S 7c  Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, and spectroscopic factors from     
 34S 8c  DWUCK-DWBA analysis.                                                   
 34S  c  1971Va21: {+33}S(d,p) with a 12-MeV deuteron beam from the Utrecht 6 MV
 34S 2c  tandem accelerator. The target was 77%-enriched {+33}S on an aluminum  
 34S 3c  backing. Reaction protons were detected using position-sensitive       
 34S 4c  detectors in the focal plane of a split-pole magnetic spectrograph.    
 34S 5c  Measured |s(E{-p},|q) from 5|' to 95|' in steps of 5|'. Deduced levels,
 34S 6c  J, |p, L-transfers, and spectroscopic factors from finite-range        
 34S 7c  DWUCK-DWBA analysis.                                                   
 34S  c  1963Br05: {+33}S(d,p) with a 6-MeV deuteron beam from the MIT-ONR      
 34S 2c  electrostatic accelerator. Targets were natural sulfur and 25%         
 34S 3c  {+33}S-enriched sulfur sublimated and layered between silver thin      
 34S 4c  films. Reaction protons were detected using nuclear emulsion plates    
 34S 5c  inside a broad-range magnetic spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-p}). Deduced
 34S 6c  23 levels.                                                             
 34S  c  1949Da16: {+33}S(d,p) with 3.22-MeV deuterons. Measured |s(E{-p}).     
 34S 2c  Deduced Q values and a 0.82-MeV level in {+34}S.                       
 34S  cL L$From 1972Cr08, unless otherwise noted.                               
 34S  cL S$From 1972Cr08 multiplied by a factor of 4. 1972Cr08 define           
 34S 2cL spectroscopic factor as:                                               
 34S 3cL C{+2}S=(2J{-i}+1)/(2J{-f}+1)|s(|q){-exp}/|s(|q){-DWBA}/N, where the    
 34S 4cL normalization factor N=1.53. J{-f} is the final spin of the 34S level  
 34S 5cL and J{-i}=3/2 is the initial spin for the target {+33} g.s.            
